<title>GREECE: Greek capital mkts commission fines shareholders.</title>
<headline>Greek capital mkts commission fines shareholders.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Greece's watchdog capital markets commission fined 24 large shareholders of Athens stock exchange listings for violating disclosure regulations on changes of ownership stakes, it said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Having reviewed 40 cases of share transactions which significantly altered ownership stakes in listed companies that were not disclosed to the Athens stock exchange within five days as the presidential decree 51/1992 requires, it fined the following 24 cases:</p>
<p>    NAME		    FINE (drs)	     STOCK</p>
<p>1.  Zoe Stegou	    1.6 million  Olympic Technical</p>
<p>2.  Piraeus Bank	  4.4 million  Piraeus Leasing</p>
<p>3.  Ag. Konstantakatos  3.4 million  Remek 4.  Zac. Kioutsoukostas 2.1 million  Kreka 5.  At. Mesochoritis   13.8 million  Mesochoritis</p>
<p>6.  K. Sarantopoulou    1.8 million  K.I.Sarandopoulos</p>
<p>7.  K. Philippou	  2.6 million  Hellenic Biscuits</p>
<p>8.  G. Bobolas	    3.3 million  Aktor</p>
<p>9.  P. Lykos		3.3 million  Inform Lykos</p>
<p>10. S. Koutla	    12.8 million  Proodeftiki</p>
<p>11. K. Halioris	   2.3 million  Mouriadis</p>
<p>12. V. Stefanis	   2.4 million  Aemet</p>
<p>13. Rokas ABEE	   10.7 million  Medinvest</p>
<p>14. Mills St.George     2.1 million  Medinvest</p>
<p>15. I.Klaoudatos	 10.3 million  Klaoudatos</p>
<p>16. Tinola Holding SA   3.0 million  Allatini</p>
<p>17. N.Ginosatis	  11.1 million  Flexopack</p>
<p>18. A. Fourlis	    2.6 million  Fourlis</p>
<p>19. N.Syrigos	    12.4 million  Athena</p>
<p>20. S. Kokkalis	  16.9 million  Intracom</p>
<p>21. Unisys Hellas	 3.5 million  Delta Inform</p>
<p>22. A. Terzi		3.7 million  Hippotour</p>
<p>23. ETBA		    3.8 million  Hellenic Invest</p>
<p>24. A. Livieratos	 2.7 million  Kekrops</p>
<p>The commission said it was still reviewing 23 other cases.</p>
<p>It said that it went easy on the magnitude of the fines as it was the first time such penalties were applied based on presidential decree 51/1992.</p>
<p>&quot;In deciding the specific fines the commission took into consideration other factors including the nature of share transfers between family members, the value of the transaction and the extent of the change in ownership,&quot; it said.</p>
<p>--George Georgiopoulos, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
